<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Jian (Former Shu)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">847–918</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Gaozu of Former Shu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Jian was a soldier of humble origin who rose in the Tang army and became military governor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a> in 891. After the Tang fell in 907 he proclaimed himself emperor of Former Shu. His wealthy state gave refuge to scholars and poets fleeing the north. His tomb at Chengdu survives with fine stone carvings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-jian-former-shu.jpg" alt="Wang Jian (Former Shu)" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Augusthaiho · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%8E%8B%E5%BB%BA%E5%83%8F03430.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
